/*
    `->` constructs a mapping, which is an ORDINARY PRODUCT: `x -> y` denotes
    `(x @ Result = y)`, fusing the left operand one level deep with a named field
    `Result` bound to the right operand.
    There is no special ordered-pair structure in Ting, and all fields of a mapping
    take part in its identity.
    Because fusion is one level deep, `(a, b) -> y` denotes `(a, b @ Result = y)`.
    A mapping on its own is not a function: `fn` turns a collection of mappings into one.
*/

1 -> 10
